2026-08-28 00:09:01 [DEBUG] llm.engine: ARGS: ('\n        You are a workflow assistant. Extract parameters for the intent "select_asset_def_by_reference".\n\n        User message:\n        select this asset -> Justice Kagan Questions Judicial Expertise\n\n        Parameter schema for this intent:\n        - "reference": type=string, required=True\n\n        Extraction instructions for this intent:\n        - The "reference" parameter must always be set to the asset\'s "title" field.\n- Never return the idea_id or quote.\n- Use the relevant context block (which lists ideas with idea_id, title, quote)\n  to determine which asset the user is referring to.\n\n\n\nRelevant context:\nasset_definitions:\n  - id: bbe44f86-ddad-46dc-9803-b626a645fc73, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Judge Chooses Statute Over Agency, quote: Skidmore deference essentially says -- and -- and we would be very comfortable\n  - id: 0663e9b6-2e28-4933-a593-18ff9ebb3bbc, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Roberts Tests Constitutional Interpretation Rules, quote: Well, what if the statute says that the agency can regulate trunk -- truck length for vehicles\n  - id: 2b7ad66c-2b4e-415f-8f78-b000c4b54e52, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Justice Kagan\'s AI Gap Hypothetical, quote: do we want courts to fill that gap, or do we want an agency to fill that gap?\n  - id: 7389d46a-7a48-475d-acb7-2ffd495b7455, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Justice Jackson\'s Implementation Dilemma, quote: going to go to court every time it gets one of these undefined terms in a statute and seek, you know, a declaratory judgment\n  - id: d1ad413a-9f16-4aea-80c0-3a36d9076e59, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Gorsuch Presses Prelogar on Empty Hands, quote: Then what?\n  - id: b2980eb2-0770-4064-83da-03b286040162, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Gorsuch Calls Chevron an Instability Recipe, quote: my good friend, but -- but Brand X is a recipe for instability,\n  - id: a9cfbef3-ae9e-4b09-b572-ca9ad0b390fc, idea_id: 22-1219, title: , quote: \n  - id: 801d8768-6c26-4945-8ad9-8e76cdcfbbeb, idea_id: 22-1219, title: , quote: \n  - id: 63ab7111-3bc5-4d51-b3ff-ecc6261a05ea, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Justice Kagan\'s Drug-Supplement Boundary Question, quote: I would rather have people at HHS telling me whether this new product was a dietary supplement or a drug.\n  - id: 8fe0e81b-3188-45c9-9078-d5106ac36048, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Justice Jackson\'s Uber-Legislator Warning, quote: when there\'s an ambiguity, there are actually different kinds of ambiguities.\n  - id: 04dc2349-cd79-4f7d-afc9-2c5b44533301, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Justice Gorsuch\'s Herring Fee Confusion Test, quote: even in a case involving herring fishermen and the question whether they have to pay for government officials to be onboard their boats,\n  - id: 372d1cee-71a0-4e71-9928-9345d12f2cea, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Alito Demands Definition for Reasonable, quote: The Court gave this definition in Kisor five years ago with respect to Auer deference, and I think it\'s the right definition to use\n  - id: 1d7219ab-9c6a-440c-9e42-b978a0dd379a, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Kavanaugh Presses Prelogar on Reasonable Gaps, quote: to borrow from the Chief Justice\'s example, reasonable truck lengths\n  - id: e6a3ebf3-a814-4c80-80dd-d324e9143592, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Roberts Tests EPA Reasonableness Limits, quote: Congress used a broad term like "appropriate" and the question was -- and -- which is similar to reasonable, in giving the agency a\n  - id: 238b6a44-d78f-46fc-a11a-eb5ff6a84ec6, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Justice Kagan Questions Judicial Expertise, quote: Will courts be able to decide these issues as to things they know nothing about,\n  - id: 6af7f314-f09a-4476-b90e-95db7a20ae05, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Martinez Invokes Chevron\'s Own Footnote, quote: is that Chevron applies in cases of ambiguity.\n  - id: 78171fd8-7f3e-4566-aee2-878c06ac18b0, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Decades of Investment at Risk, quote: People have made investment decisions on the basis of that.\n  - id: c975c981-4c38-4a9f-8d84-a96ab6386bc9, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Chevron\'s Encouraged Flip-Flop Feature, quote: it encourages and allows agencies to flip-flop. And\n  - id: 4ee1d645-8cad-43f9-96c5-e3980c931ae0, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Congress Waits While Chevron Grows, quote: considered proposals to do so, but it\'s never taken that step. Instead, Congress has legislated for decades with Chevron as the background rule informing\n  - id: f4ad0b91-a0d9-4f67-a6f9-543240d707cd, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Justice Kavanaugh\'s Dual-Context Test, quote: And in that context, if Congress has given the agency this primary critically important role to administer the statute, that should merit deference\n  - id: ac12e5be-bfe7-40fa-8adb-44b46abf7a9b, idea_id: 22-1219, title: Martinez\'s Fishermen Profit Hypothetical, quote: struggling fishermen to pay up to 20 percent of their annual profits to federal agents.\n\nFollow these rules:\n- Extract parameters strictly according to the schema.\n- Apply the extraction instructions above.\n- Use context only when the user refers indirectly (e.g., "it", "that one").\n- If a parameter cannot be extracted, set it to null.\n- Return ONLY valid JSON. No commentary.\n\nReturn JSON in this format:\n{\n    "parameters": {\n        <param_name>: <value or null>\n    },\n    "reasoning": "<brief explanation>"\n}\n',)
